{"algorithm":"ML-KEM","schema":"mlkem_test_schema.json","numberOfTests":201,"notes":{"Strcmp":{"bugType":"CAN_OF_WORMS","description":"In ML-KEM.Decaps the ciphertext is compared with the output of K-PKE.Encrypt for implicit rejection. If an implementation were to use strcmp() for that comparison it would fail to reject some ciphertexts if a zero byte terminates the comparison early. The chance of it occurring randomly is 2⁻¹⁶. These vectors are valid and test that the implicit rejection path is taken as expected."},"MalleableCiphertext":{"bugType":"CAN_OF_WORMS","description":"The ciphertext is malleable."}},"testGroups":[{"type":"MLKEMTest","source":{"name":"CCTV/strcmp","version":"0.1"},"parameterSet":"ML-KEM-768","tests":[{"tcId":1,"flags":["Strcmp"],"seed":"cbfc4405d1b2a3a386c94c25e0f2d5f5ee92cb0388ff4d6aa04223086d51c3fd24752da14c9fc3b8ae0d9e4a8b1016b8d8fc69e229c03ea2ef08a4ae0cffc37f","ek":"","c":"","K":"76c10bb1d86d96d7eb18e298363e51f7728e113f455df7d15017940ed3541451","result":"valid"}]},{"type":"MLKEMTest","source":{"name":"FIPS 203","version":"1.0"},"parameterSet":"ML-KEM-768","tests":[{"tcId":2,"comment":"Test vector based on official round 3 seeds 0","flags":[],"seed":"7c9935a0b07694aa0c6d10e4db6b1add2fd81a25ccb148032dcd739936737f2d8626ed79d451140800e03b59b956f8210e556067407d13dc90fa9e8b872bfb8f","ek":"","c":"","K":"e7184a0975ee3470878d2d159ec83129c8aec253d4ee17b4810311d198cd0368","result":"valid"},{"tcId":102,"comment":"Private key too short","flags":[],"seed":"eee085b14cd41ff696aabf2d9c7f613aa6edcb8f87a39b8772de8784b4","c":"","K":"","result":"invalid"}]},{"type":"MLKEMTest","source":{"name":"github.com/007bsd/mlkem-implicit-rejection","version":"1"},"parameterSet":"ML-KEM-768","tests":[{"tcId":194,"comment":"Ciphertext modified at byte 0 (c1 poly-block 0); implicit rejection must fire, so a re-encryption comparison that skips this position is detected","flags":["MalleableCiphertext"],"seed":"7c9935a0b07694aa0c6d10e4db6b1add2fd81a25ccb148032dcd739936737f2